# Netlify publishes this repository from its root, so every committed file is a
# candidate for being served. Proved Sep 21, 2026: /supabase-schema.sql returned
# 200 on the live site. specs/ had not deployed yet only because the live build
# predated the commit that added it, which is luck rather than protection.
#
# These rules are that protection. Anything internal gets a 404, and the
# stylesheet and nav beside the specs go with them so the folder is not
# partially readable.
/specs/*              /404.html  404
/scripts/*            /404.html  404
/CLAUDE.md            /404.html  404
/supabase-schema.sql  /404.html  404
/package.json         /404.html  404
/package-lock.json    /404.html  404
/netlify.toml         /404.html  404
